---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Common Questions | Quiet Grid Press"
  description="Answers to common questions about Quiet Grid Press puzzle books: where to buy, the Bible Verse Sudoku series, difficulty, answers, and orders."
>
  <section class="page-intro paper-texture">
    <div class="shell narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Helpful Answers</p>
      <h1>Common Questions</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        These answers cover the questions we can resolve clearly today. New
        or unusual questions will be reviewed personally.
      </p>
      <div class="button-row centered-buttons">
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="/contact/">Ask a Question</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell faq">
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details>
          <summary>Where can I buy Quiet Grid Press books?</summary>
          <p>
            Quiet Grid Press books are paperbacks sold on Amazon. Every book is
            listed on our <a href="/books/">Books page</a>, where each one is
            marked Now Available or Coming soon, and the button on a book's
            own page opens that book on Amazon.
            <a
              class="text-link"
              href="/amazon/bible-verse-sudoku/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              data-track="amazon-outbound"
            >
              View Bible Verse Sudoku on Amazon <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How many books are in the Bible Verse Sudoku series?</summary>
          <p>
            Seven collections. Each one pairs 120 Easy puzzles with 120 verses,
            one puzzle to a page. The
            <a href="/books/">Books page</a> shows which are Now Available and
            which are Coming soon.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Which Bible translation do the Bible Verse Sudoku books use?</summary>
          <p>
            The King James Version. Each verse is printed exactly, with its
            chapter and verse.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What does Easy mean?</summary>
          <p>
            In our books, an Easy puzzle can be finished with plain logic:
            scanning rows, columns, and boxes, and finding the square that can
            only hold one number. No guessing. In the Bible Verse Sudoku books
            the label is printed at the foot of every puzzle page.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What difficulty levels are the puzzles?</summary>
          <p>
            Every puzzle in the Bible Verse Sudoku books is Easy. USA250 Sudoku
            progresses through Easy, Medium, and Hard puzzles.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does every puzzle have exactly one solution?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. Every puzzle is checked to have exactly one solution before it
            goes into a book.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Are answers included?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. Each Bible Verse Sudoku book has complete solutions in the
            back, six to a page. USA250 Sudoku includes a complete answer
            section for all 250 puzzles.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How big are the books?</summary>
          <p>
            Each Bible Verse Sudoku book is a paperback of 158 pages. Amazon
            lists its size as 8.5 x 0.38 x 11 inches: a page 8.5 inches wide
            and 11 inches tall, in a book a little over a third of an inch
            thick. A book with more puzzles is thicker; each book's Amazon page
            gives its own size.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How much room is there to work a puzzle?</summary>
          <p>
            In the Bible Verse Sudoku books every puzzle has a page to itself.
            The grid is 6.2 inches wide, so each square is about two-thirds of
            an inch across, and the numbers already in the grid are printed at
            26 point. There is open space around the grid for your own notes.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Are these large-print books?</summary>
          <p>
            No. Large print is the name libraries and publishers use for books
            whose reading text is set in type of about 16 to 18 points. The
            words in our books, such as the instructions and the verse beside
            each puzzle, are set at 12 and 13 points, so we do not call them
            large print, and we do not publish a large-print edition at this
            time. What the books do offer is room: one puzzle to a page, a
            grid 6.2 inches wide, and grid numbers printed at 26 point.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Who handles orders, delivery, returns, or damaged copies?</summary>
          <p>
            Amazon handles purchasing, delivery, returns, and order support for
            books purchased through its store. Please use the support options
            connected to your Amazon order.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
